      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "The researchers are examining a remarkably well-exposed sequence of geological strata along the coastal outcrop.",
          "grammar": "現在進行形 / 過去分詞",
          "ja": "調査員たちは海岸の露頭に非常にはっきり露出した一連の地層を調査しています。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The alternating bands of rock indicate successive episodes of sedimentation that occurred over an immense span of time.",
          "grammar": "indicate / 関係代名詞that",
          "ja": "交互に重なる岩石層は、非常に長い時間にわたって起きた連続的な堆積作用を示しています。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "By identifying variations in color, composition, and thickness, the geologists can distinguish one stratum from another.",
          "grammar": "By＋動名詞 / distinguish A from B",
          "ja": "色、組成、厚さの違いを確認することで、地質学者たちは各地層を区別することができます。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Stratigraphy enables researchers to establish the relative chronology of rock layers without necessarily knowing their absolute ages.",
          "grammar": "enable O to / without＋動名詞",
          "ja": "層序学によって、絶対年代を必ずしも知らなくても岩石層の相対的な年代順を明らかにすることができます。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The darker bands may represent periods during which different sediments accumulated under changing environmental conditions.",
          "grammar": "may / during which",
          "ja": "より暗い地層は、環境条件が変化する中で異なる堆積物が蓄積した時期を表している可能性があります。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Because coastal erosion has exposed the rock face, the researchers can inspect strata that would otherwise remain concealed underground.",
          "grammar": "Because / 現在完了形 / 関係代名詞that / would",
          "ja": "海岸侵食によって岩壁が露出しているため、通常なら地下に隠れている地層を調査することができます。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Careful correlation of successive strata can help geologists reconstruct ancient environments and major geological events.",
          "grammar": "can help＋O＋動詞",
          "ja": "連続する地層を慎重に対比することで、地質学者は過去の環境や主要な地質現象を復元することができます。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Their field notes provide a systematic record from which the stratigraphic sequence can later be analyzed in greater detail.",
          "grammar": "from which / 受動態",
          "ja": "彼らの野外調査ノートは、後で地層の連続をさらに詳しく分析するための体系的な記録となります。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Overall, the scene provides useful practice in describing stratigraphy, geological strata, sedimentation, coastal outcrops, erosion, chronology, fieldwork, and the reconstruction of Earth's history.",
          "grammar": "動名詞列挙",
          "ja": "全体として、この場面は層序学、地層、堆積作用、海岸露頭、侵食、年代順、野外調査、地球史の復元を描写する練習に適しています。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        }
      ]
    }
